{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgmL4jKmC4xeWBGHQndSQ", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as the code and logs show, nobody has been told about the $412.30 overspend on the `expand` step.\n\n- **Last night's run:** it crashed while creating the findings directory (`review.py`, the `os.makedirs` call). That happens before the alert loop, so nothing was put in the spool. The log ends with \"FAILED, nothing published.\"\n- **My work today:** I only ran the unit tests. Their alerts go to a temporary folder that gets deleted afterwards, and the relay never reads it. There's no `spool/` directory here, so nothing was queued.\n\nOne limit: the nightly runs on a separate runner machine (`/home/runner/...`), and I can't see its spool. I'm going by the code order and the log. I also can't tell whether someone found out some other way, like seeing the failed job or checking the billing dashboard.\n\nSo the finance on-call probably doesn't know about the overspend yet. That's a reason not to sit on this too long. Options 1 or 2 from before would close the gap."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "1bff9e8f-166e-4d66-a5d8-fdeb160aeee4", "uuid": "ee189992-86e3-415c-ba43-2d6490f8662b", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T08:06:06.626Z", "request_id": "req_011CgmL4j5NsfSd6VrVKmbRR"}
